[ti:Royal Espionage]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.39]Lesson 9 | 第9课
[00:02.28]Royal espionage | 王室谍报活动
[00:11.31]What important thing did King Alfred learn when he penetrated the Danish camp of Guthrum? | 阿尔弗雷德大王潜入古斯鲁姆的丹麦军营时，获知了什么重要情报？
[00:20.72]Alfred the Great acted as his own spy, visiting Danish camps disguised as a minstrel. | 阿尔弗雷德大王曾亲自充当间谍，扮成吟游歌手深入丹麦军营。
[00:29.54]In those days wandering minstrels were welcome everywhere. | 在那个年代，流浪的吟游歌手到处受到欢迎。
[00:34.45]They were not fighting men, and their harp was their passport. | 他们不是作战人员，竖琴就是他们的通行证。
[00:39.20]Alfred had learned many of their ballads in his youth and could vary his programme with acrobatic tricks and simple conjuring. | 阿尔弗雷德年轻时学会了许多他们的民歌，还能用杂技和简单的戏法变换自己的表演节目。
[00:49.17]While Alfred's little army slowly began to gather at Athelney, the king himself set out to penetrate the camp of Guthrum, the commander of the Danish invaders. | 在阿尔弗雷德的小部队慢慢集结于阿塞尔奈的时候，国王亲自出马，潜入丹麦侵略军司令官古斯鲁姆的营地。
[01:02.26]These had settled down for the winter at Chippenham: thither Alfred went. | 丹麦人已在奇彭纳姆安营扎寨过冬，阿尔弗雷德便前往该地。
[01:09.32]He noticed at once that discipline was slack: the Danes had the self-confidence of conquerors, and their security precautions were casual. | 他立刻发现丹麦军纪涣散：他们以征服者自居，戒备松懈。
[01:21.06]They lived well, on the proceeds of raids on neighbouring regions. | 他们靠掠夺邻近地区而生活优裕。
[01:26.77]There they collected women as well as food and drink, and a life of ease had made them soft. | 他们在那里不仅收集食物和酒，还收集女人，安逸的生活已使他们变得软弱。
[01:34.89]Alfred stayed in the camp a week before he returned to Athelney. | 阿尔弗雷德在军营中待了一个星期后，回到了阿塞尔奈。
[01:40.13]The force there assembled was trivial compared with the Danish horde. | 那里集结的兵力与丹麦大军相比微不足道。
[01:45.12]But Alfred had deduced that the Danes were no longer fit for prolonged battle: and that their commissariat had no organization, but depended on irregular raids. | 但阿尔弗雷德推断，丹麦人已不再适宜打持久战：而且他们的给养系统毫无组织，全靠不时地抢劫。
[01:58.52]So, faced with the Danish advance, Alfred did not risk open battle but harried the enemy. | 所以，面对丹麦人的推进，阿尔弗雷德没有贸然正面交锋，而是袭扰敌军。
[02:06.57]He was constantly on the move, drawing the Danes after him. | 他不停地转移，把丹麦人拖在身后。
[02:11.58]His patrols halted the raiding parties: hunger assailed the Danish army. | 他的巡逻队拦截了敌人的抢掠队伍：饥饿袭击着丹麦军队。
[02:17.97]Now Alfred began a long series of skirmishes -- and within a month the Danes had surrendered. | 这时阿尔弗雷德开始了一系列长期的游击战斗——不到一个月，丹麦人就投降了。
[02:25.74]The episode could reasonably serve as a unique epic of royal espionage! | 这一段历史完全可以称得上是王室谍报活动的一则独一无二的史诗！
